Stores historical and current exchange rates between currencies, enabling accurate multi-currency conversions at specific dates.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Daily / manual exchange rate updates
Automatic rate fetching from external providers (ECB, Yahoo, etc.)
Date-specific conversions for invoices, payments, journal entries, and bank statements
Historical rate lookup for reporting and revaluation
Multi-company rate management
Currency gain/loss calculation on reconciliation and payments

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent, lightweight)
Key Fields:
name (date, required) – the rate date
currency_id → res.currency (required)
rate (float, required) – rate against company currency (e.g. 1 USD = 15,800 IDR)
company_id (optional — allows different rates per company)
inverse_company_rate / rate (computed inverses)

Critical Hooks: _compute_rate, create, rate uniqueness constraint per (currency, date, company)
Security: account.group_account_manager for write access

RAG Routing Keywords:
currency rate, exchange rate, forex rate, currency conversion rate, res.currency.rate, rate history, historical rate, exchange rate on date, rate update, currency revaluation, daily rate
Related Models (most joined):

res.currency (parent)
res.company (company currency)
account.move.line (via currency_id + date)
account.payment, account.bank.statement.line
sale.order, purchase.order, pos.order

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
res.currency.rate is the child model of res.currency that stores dated exchange rates (name=date, rate value, currency_id, company_id). It powers all multi-currency conversions, automatic rate application on documents, historical lookups, currency gain/loss entries, and revaluation processes throughout Odoo accounting, sales, purchase, and reporting.